The physician’s role in this approach is to:
- evaluate fatigue, poor recovery, or reduced performance and frame the findings as iron deficiency, anemia, or another treatable cause when documentation support is needed;
- prescribe and document treatment in a way that is consistent across the chart, prescription record, and any follow-up notes;
- if questions arise, rely on the existence of symptoms, prior labs, and clinical discretion rather than volunteering performance-related intent;
- coordinate legal supplements, nutrition planning, altitude exposure where permitted, sleep optimization, hydration, and recovery strategies around the EPO course.

